<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14810" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dryas</span></b> , antis,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δρύας</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The father of Lycurgus king of Thrace</i>, <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab.
				132</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Serv. Verg. A. 3,
			14</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dryantīdes</span></b> , ae,
				m., i. e. <i>Lycurgus</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. Ib.
			347</span></i>; cf. Hyg. and <i><span class="en">Serv. 1</span></i>.
			1.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>One of the Lapithae</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
				12, 290 sq.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A sharer in the Calydonican hunt</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 8,
				307</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
